-- A COMPUTED field whose body reads a section binder.
--
-- The evaluator desugars `x's tax` to an application of the field's selector,
-- which is an ordinary module-level definition; so a computed field that reads
-- a binder is discharged exactly like any other rule, and the projection site
-- has to grow the same arguments a call site does.
--
-- This is a separate code path from the plain call in
-- ok/section-given-discharge.l4 (`Proj` rather than `App`/`Var`), which is why
-- it has a file of its own.

§ `Rates`
    GIVEN `the rate` IS A NUMBER TYPICALLY 0.05

DECLARE Sale
    HAS amount IS A NUMBER
        tax    IS A NUMBER MEANS amount TIMES `the rate`

GIVETH A NUMBER
`tax of the sample sale` MEANS (Sale WITH amount IS 100)'s tax

-- Supplied at the call: the value reaches the field's own body.
#EVAL `tax of the sample sale` WITH `the rate` IS 0.07

-- Nothing supplied: the binder's TYPICALLY is filled in at the root, and the
-- computed field sees it.
#EVAL `tax of the sample sale`

-- `WITH` attaches to a NAME, not to an arbitrary expression, so a projection
-- cannot carry one directly: `(Sale WITH amount IS 200)'s tax WITH ...` is a
-- parse error ("unexpected WITH"). Supply the binder at a rule that wraps the
-- projection, as `tax of the sample sale` does above.

#ASSERT (`tax of the sample sale` WITH `the rate` IS 0.07) EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `tax of the sample sale` EQUALS 5
